## Workflow — run this FIRST (any project/task)

Before writing any code, follow the **superpowers** workflow (obra/superpowers): **brainstorming** → **using-git-worktrees** → **writing-plans** → build with **test-driven-development** → **requesting-code-review** → **verification-before-completion**. Do NOT jump straight into code.

Read before working in this repo:

- [`docs/architecture.md`](docs/architecture.md) — stack, folder layout, DI, state management, networking, error model. Read before adding a feature, touching cross-cutting code (`lib/core/`), or wiring anything into the app entry point.
- [`docs/rules.md`](docs/rules.md) — naming conventions, layer rules, testing, and the definition-of-done checklist. Read before writing or reviewing any Dart code, and before implementing a Figma design (§13 covers Figma-MCP UI slicing).
- [`docs/design.md`](docs/design.md) — visual design system: colors, typography, spacing, and component tokens. Read before styling any widget or implementing a Figma design, alongside `rules.md` §13.

